fail b.cue
exit 1

The module is older than the experiments' preview versions, so there is
no "stay at this version" conversion to offer: the report says so instead
of printing a cue fix command that would be refused.

-- cue.mod/module.cue --
module: "mod.test"

language: version: "v0.9.0"

-- a.cue --
package p

X=a: {b: X.c, c: 1}
-- b.cue --
package p

Y=b: {c: Y.d, d: 1}
-- expect/stderr --
b.cue:1:1: injected rewrite failure
mod upgrade: 1 file(s) could not be converted; nothing written, language version left at v0.9.0
    v0.9.0 cannot carry @experiment attributes for aliasv2,explicitopen: fix the files above by hand, then run the upgrade again
    to upgrade anyway, leaving those files invalid at v0.18.0:
        cue mod upgrade --force v0.18.0
